  "narrative": "Compared to last week's sale steer calves under 400 lbs sold 35.00-40.00 lower, 400-499 lbs mostly 10.00 lower. Heavier steer calves 500-699 lbs sold 9.00-13.00 higher. Feeder steers 700-899 lbs not enough to establish a market trend. Feeder heifers 350-499 lbs sold uneven at 5.00 lower to 5.00 higher, 500-699 lb heifers sold 7.00-9.00 lower. Not enough heavier heifers for price comparison. Compared to the Wednesday sale, slaughter and return to feed cows traded 2.00-3.00 lower. Supply included: 89% Feeder Cattle (57% Steers, 43% Heifers, 0% Bulls); 6% Slaughter Cattle (90% Cows, 10% Bulls); 5% Replacement Cattle (76% Stock Cows, 9% Bred Cows, 15% Open Heifers). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 25%.",
